Task 3: Review the Structure of Camel Routes and Components
Subtask 3.1: Analyze Route Components
Let's break down the components of our Camel routes:

Route Structure Analysis
From Endpoint (Consumer):

from("file:data/input?noop=true") - Polls the input directory for files
from("timer:hello?period=5000") - Triggers every 5 seconds
Processing Steps (Processors):

.log() - Logs messages to console
.setBody() - Sets the message body content
To Endpoint (Producer):

to("file:data/output") - Writes files to output directory
Subtask 3.2: Create an Advanced Route with Transformations
Create a new RouteBuilder for advanced scenarios:
touch src/main/java/com/alnafi/camel/lab2/routes/AdvancedRoute.java
Add the following code:
package com.alnafi.camel.lab2.routes;

import org.apache.camel.builder.RouteBuilder;

/**
 * Advanced Camel route demonstrating message transformation and routing
 */
public class AdvancedRoute extends RouteBuilder {
    
    @Override
    public void configure() throws Exception {
        
        // Route 3: Content-based routing with transformation
        from("file:data/input/orders?noop=true")
            .log("Processing order file: ${header.CamelFileName}")
            .choice()
                .when(header("CamelFileName").endsWith(".xml"))
                    .log("Processing XML order")
                    .transform(body().prepend("XML Order processed at ${date:now}: "))
                    .to("file:data/output/xml-orders")
                .when(header("CamelFileName").endsWith(".json"))
                    .log("Processing JSON order")
                    .transform(body().prepend("JSON Order processed at ${date:now}: "))
                    .to("file:data/output/json-orders")
                .otherwise()
                    .log("Processing generic order")
                    .transform(body().prepend("Generic Order processed at ${date:now}: "))
                    .to("file:data/output/generic-orders");
                    
        // Route 4: Message filtering and aggregation
        from("timer:stats?period=10000")
            .setBody(constant("System Status: OK - Memory: ${sys.java.runtime.freememory} bytes"))
            .log("System stats: ${body}")
            .to("file:data/output/stats?fileName=system-stats-${date:now:yyyyMMdd-HHmmss}.log");
    }
}
